------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Open data attribution
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This software fetches, parses and redistributes derived figures from French and
European public data. The source data remains under its own licence and the
attribution below is required wherever those figures are shown. The application
footer, the README and docs/DATA_SOURCES.md all carry it.

  * Agreste — Statistique Agricole Annuelle, long series 2010-2024.
    Ministère de l'Agriculture et de la Souveraineté alimentaire (France).
    Licence Ouverte / Open Licence (Etalab).

  * Météo-France — Données climatologiques de base, mensuelles, par station.
    Licence Ouverte / Open Licence (Etalab).

  * IGN — API Carto, Registre Parcellaire Graphique (RPG) v2, and
    ADMIN EXPRESS commune geometry.
    Licence Ouverte / Open Licence (Etalab).

  * ADEME — Agribalyse, agricultural life-cycle impact data.
    Licence Ouverte / Open Licence (Etalab).

  * Eurostat — agricultural price indices (apri_ap_crpouta). Used only for a
    documented validation check; the series was found NOT USABLE for this
    purpose and is not relied on. See data/processed/price_validation.json.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data that is NOT open data, and is NOT real
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * Buyer contract terms (backend/app/refdata/buyers.json) — prices, volumes
    and premiums are illustrative demo data. They are not commercial offers and
    no named counterparty has agreed to them.

  * The livestock holding directory (backend/app/refdata/breeders.json) — the
    commune centroids are real IGN geography and the count per department is
    scaled by a measured land-use ratio, but holding names, herd types and herd
    sizes are generated with a fixed seed. No real farm is described.

Both are labelled as demo data everywhere they surface in the API and the UI.
